00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:22.069
And quick heads up on future spoilers.

00:01:22.069 --> 00:01:24.569
I don't consider any of the stuff I'm going
to talk about to be major spoilers for the

00:01:24.569 --> 00:01:26.600
books or anything.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:33.079
Most of all my conclusions are based on contextual
clues from season 4 episodes.

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:36.799
Especially the big changes Dan and Dave made.

00:01:36.799 --> 00:01:40.920
So here we go, starting with Tyrion and Varys
who are basically travel companions now.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:45.159
There were a few callbacks to season 2 and
3 scenes in their final moments.

00:01:45.159 --> 00:01:46.159
First was the Box.

00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:48.200
All I could think about was Varys Sorcerer
that he captured.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.169
That was the exact same type of box.

00:01:51.169 --> 00:01:53.689
Then there was the bells.

00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:58.179
Back during Blackwater, Varys said he always
hated the bells because they always ring for

00:01:58.179 --> 00:01:59.329
horror.

00:01:59.329 --> 00:02:02.069
Like a dead king or a city under seige.

00:02:02.069 --> 00:02:06.689
Tyrion joked that they also ring for weddings,
which I guess you could consider a moment

00:02:06.689 --> 00:02:10.229
of foreshadowing for the red wedding, which
hadn't happened at that point.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.890
Weddings on Game of Thrones are pretty horrific.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:16.700
The boat they're on is headed east, because
there's not really anywhere in Westeros they'd

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:17.880
be safe after what happened.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.000
Varys probably would have been fine, but remember
how hard he's been working to strengthen the

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.000
realm.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.640
Cersei is in charge again now that Tywin is
gone.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:29.040
She won't have to marry Loras and Twyin won't
be there to stop her from indulging every

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.040
whim.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:35.940
She's not a monster like Joffrey, but she
is a really selfish person.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.300
And now she has free reign.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.840
Number 2 - Cersei and Jaime

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:43.320
Cersei as discussed will figure out that she's
in charge again and put the brakes on anything

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.690
she doesn't like.

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:48.190
On the bonus side, she'll be able to spend
all her time watching over Tommen and Ser

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.210
Pounce.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:52.630
I'll say Ser Pounce is someone I hope the
include at least once next year.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:57.280
The director of that episode said to not expect
him back, but I think it would be a lot of

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.280
fun.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:03.941
Jaime looks like he's still stuck between
wanting to do great deeds worthy of the White

00:03:03.941 --> 00:03:09.570
Book and his love for Cersei.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:22.020
It's a pretty toxic love so I fully expect
him to continue flip flop back 

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.220
and forth.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:28.730
Number 3 - Up at the Wall, Stannis, Melisandre
and Jon Snow

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:32.230
Stannis has a massive army there now, paid
for with the Iron Bank's money.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.230
A lot of their money.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:36.700
His army is big enough to man some of the
other castles along the wall.

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:40.370
So I really hope they build sets for those
locations, like the Night Fort.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:47.260
It's possible that they could just spend the
entire season just at Castle Black too.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:52.990
Melisandre gave Jon that long stare through
the flames.

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:56.330
Anytime she stares at someone it either means
she's going to have sex with them at some

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:59.040
point or use them in some horrific plot.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.220
Or in the case of Gendry, both.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.320
For now it just seems like she's going to
shift her focus to him.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.209
We don't really know what she's planning with
Shireen.

00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:06.620
Even though we didn't see her in the episode
remember how she insisted that Stannis bring

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:07.620
her to The Wall with them.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.380
Melisandre has always said that Stannis was
Azor Ahai but I'd love to see her put that

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:12.760
on Jon Snow.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:17.259
He and Stannis shared that long look of understanding
about burning the bodies so he understands

00:04:17.259 --> 00:04:18.349
the threat of the white walkers.

00:04:18.349 --> 00:04:23.449
But I don't expect Jon to completely buy into
anything Melisandre might see in the flames

00:04:23.449 --> 00:04:24.930
as regards him.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:31.479
Remember, Jojen said that only the green dreams
always come true.

00:04:31.479 --> 00:04:34.229
Visions in the flames can be things that might
have happened, they're not always things that

00:04:34.229 --> 00:04:35.520
will happen.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:37.080
Number 4 - On to Bran's Group

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:40.300
It seemed like a lot of you guys were more
interested in talking about Jojen's death

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:44.509
as it affects the story more than what was
going on with Bran so I'll start with that.

00:04:44.509 --> 00:04:47.949
All of the Jojen stuff that happens in the
books after they arrive at the tree is in

00:04:47.949 --> 00:04:51.830
Dance with Dragons so Bran's story on the
show was taken a lot from that book.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:54.560
He doesn't really appear in book 4.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.910
Books 4 and 5 occur during the same time period
though.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.599
So think of it as one giant book split in
half.

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:03.419
In the book Jojen still has visions of his
death, it just happens in a different way,

00:05:03.419 --> 00:05:07.319
so on the show when the Three Eye Raven said
that Jojen always knew he was going to die,

00:05:07.319 --> 00:05:09.889
he was acknowledging that fate.

00:05:09.889 --> 00:05:13.419
I think the show changed his death just because
it was more efficient and they didn't want

00:05:13.419 --> 00:05:15.069
to include his character next season.

00:05:15.069 --> 00:05:19.139
But from a story standpoint, he'd served his
purpose, he was only there to help Bran reach

00:05:19.139 --> 00:05:21.689
the Three Eye Raven, which he did.

00:05:21.689 --> 00:05:24.729
As for Meera, she's basically done too.

00:05:24.729 --> 00:05:29.069
She was mostly Jojen's caregiver, since she's
still alive I think she'll stay and help Bran

00:05:29.069 --> 00:05:33.960
with Hodor, although Bran won't really need
Hodor as much since they're in that cave now.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:39.129
The Child of the Forest is kind of like the
Hodor for the Three Eyed Raven, just serving

00:05:39.129 --> 00:05:43.259
support functions.

00:05:43.259 --> 00:05:45.310
Number 5 - Arya Stark

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:47.860
She's one of the few characters that's on
her own.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.590
Gendry is the other big one that comes to
mind.

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:53.580
Just someone who isn't traveling with another
main character.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:06:01.469
Her ship is headed to Braavos, so she's probably
going to pick up where she left off with Jaquen

00:06:01.469 --> 00:06:02.509
H'gar.

00:06:02.509 --> 00:06:06.160
